  }

The write is unconditional — the only guard is os.UserHomeDir() succeeding; there is no debug/verbose env check, no early return between this and the effort-persist block above it. The comment self-identifies it as a debug inspection file. git diff confirms the dimension label: these are `+` lines in the uncommitted working tree (not present in HEAD:statusline.go), so "uncommitted-diff" is correct. cmdStatusline is the statusline hook entrypoint (reads stdin, renders the line), so it does run on every statusline refresh.

So the core assertion — an always-on debug stdin dump that should be gated — is real and the proposed fix (wrap in `if os.Getenv("PERISCOPE_DEBUG") != ""`) is correct and sufficient.

